# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# AI coding-tool state. Per-developer, per-machine, and none of it is a project
# decision — the interpreter paths differ between checkouts and the preference
# notes are about a person, not the software.
#
# ⚠ Whole directories, not named files. The previous version ignored
# `.claude/launch.json` and `.claude/settings.local.json` individually, so
# anything else these tools wrote into those folders was fair game for
# `git add -A` — which is exactly how `.commandcode/` ended up tracked and
# public, including a file of inferred notes about how the author likes to work.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.claude/
.commandcode/
.aider*
.cursor/

/backups/

# Tailwind's toolchain. ⚠ static/css/tailwind.css is the *compiled* output but is
# deliberately NOT ignored — it is the stylesheet the app serves, and the CSP
# forbids a runtime CDN, so a checkout with no Node installed still has to be
# able to render. Rebuild it with `npm run build:css` after editing any template.
/node_modules/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OS and editor noise. ⚠ Not hypothetical: this repository has been through a
# Windows checkout on an NTFS/DrvFs mount (see TODO.md), so Thumbs.db and
# desktop.ini are live risks rather than boilerplate.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
*.swp
*~

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local handoff notes. ⚠ Deliberately untracked: it carries machine paths and a
# throwaway development password, and it describes the working session rather
# than the product. The tracked equivalents are TODO.md and project_plan.md.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/HANDOFF.md
